      "assessment": "The three studies in Philosophia Scientiæ 30-3 examine historical definitions of materialism within the French philosophical disputes covered by the issue. The English text correctly distinguishes Bernard-Granger’s interpretation of Schelling’s reception, Leonardi’s account of Bonald’s treatment of materialism, and Barancy’s analysis of Laromiguière. The November 4 primary-window edition contributes one issue-level example. Earlier editions with the same papers contribute no additional independent evidence."
